Living truthfully and faithfully into the reality as it is.

478
00:39:29,560 --> 00:39:31,140
It is beautiful but broken.

479
00:39:31,140 --> 00:39:34,300
God has triumphed, but we wait his final victory.

480
00:39:34,300 --> 00:39:39,680
We have been saved and restored, but we still experience pain, loss, and death.

481
00:39:39,680 --> 00:39:45,540
We cannot deny any aspect of our reality, neither negative or positive.

482
00:39:45,540 --> 00:39:49,100
In the face of brokenness, we lament, we grieve, and we mourn.

483
00:39:49,100 --> 00:39:52,700
And yet we celebrate because we are God's people.

484
00:39:52,700 --> 00:39:57,880
And celebrating, rejoicing, having joy is an act of defiant faith.

485
00:39:57,880 --> 00:40:07,880
Your capacity for joy is directly connected to the amount of God's grace and truth that you choose to acknowledge and receive.

486
00:40:07,960 --> 00:40:09,940
I heard a pastor say it this way this week.

487
00:40:09,940 --> 00:40:14,720
What happens to us does not have to define what happens in us.

488
00:40:14,720 --> 00:40:20,840
What happens to us does not have to define what happens in us.

489
00:40:22,740 --> 00:40:26,780
Christian, the world needs no more Debbie Downers.

490
00:40:26,780 --> 00:40:29,120
I mean, no more fake Franks.

491
00:40:29,120 --> 00:40:37,700
The world needs real people with real lives, the people of God, to acknowledge the brokenness of this world and to step into it with compassion and grace.

492
00:40:38,340 --> 00:40:46,580
A people who are honest about the world as it is, but have a deep sense of joy because we have the faith to see what the world will be.

493
00:40:46,580 --> 00:40:52,700
This type of joy has power to transform communities.

494
00:40:52,700 --> 00:41:01,720
This type of joy brings visible, tangible expressions of God's kingdom on earth as it is in heaven.

